<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mihirakula</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mihirakula was a ruler of the Alchon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> who controlled parts of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the early sixth century. He is remembered in Indian sources as a cruel persecutor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>. Hunnic invasions under rulers such as Mihirakula contributed to the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mihirakula.jpg" alt="Mihirakula" width="320" height="342" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG coins. Contoured by me पाटलिपुत्र (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mihirakula_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
